// `compositor SOCKET KEYMAP LAUNCH-DIR [W H] [--screens WxH,...] [--xwayland] [--screen] [--input FILE] [--check]`: a Wayland compositor in Coax (docs/os/2026-10-30-coderos-and-coax-audit.md,
// step 2 row 6). It serves real Wayland clients on SOCKET (WAYLAND_DISPLAY may name it as a full path):
// wl_compositor, wl_subcompositor, wl_shm, wl_seat, wl_output, wl_data_device_manager (the clipboard),
// zxdg_decoration_manager_v1 (server-side: the compositor draws the borders) and xdg_wm_base, and it places every
// toplevel with os/wm.coax, the CoderOS window policy, on one W x H screen (1280 x 720 when not given).
// The CoderOS key bindings run first (Super+Return opens Coder, Super+arrows move the focus, and the
// rest of Omarchy's tiling keys); a binding that starts a program runs LAUNCH-DIR/NAME with NAME one
// of coder, pane, dictation, presentation, browser, android, camera. Super+Shift+E leaves.
// LAUNCH-DIR/start, when there is one, runs once the socket is up: the session's start list.
// KEYMAP is the XKB keymap text clients get (os/compositor-us.xkb is the US layout, compiled once by
// `xkbcli compile-keymap --layout us`; it is data, not a tool).
// With --screen it takes the first connected screen through KMS (from a free VT; Ctrl+Alt+Backspace
// leaves and puts the screen back) and grabs the keyboards and mice. Without it, it is headless.
// On a VT it owns switching: Ctrl+Alt+F1..F12 shows that VT, and the screen and the devices are let
// go while another VT shows (another session takes them back). --leave-to N shows VT N on leaving.
// --input FILE plays a file of evdev records through the same path, on the file's own clock.
// Either way a test channel on stdin, one command a line, answered on stdout:
//   list                     every window: id, desk, rectangle in pixels, focus, app id, title
//   shot PATH                composites the screen and writes it to PATH as a PPM image
//   frame PATH               draws only what changed since the last picture, then writes it (checks damage)
//   move X Y | click         the pointer: moves (focus follows it, as Hyprland's follow_mouse) or clicks
//   key CODE | text TEXT     a key by evdev code, or US-layout text, through the bindings
//   chord CODE...            keys pressed in order and released in reverse (125 is Super)
//   keydown CODE 0|1 | button CODE 0|1 | mouse DX DY    raw input, as the devices send it
//   close                    asks the focused window to close
//   wm OP [ARG]              a window-policy verb: movefocus D, movewindow D, resize D F, togglesplit,
//                            togglefloating, fullscreen, maximize, switch N, moveto N (D 0..3 left
//                            right up down, N 0..8)
//   pointer on|off           draws the pointer in headless shots too
//   bench N                  composites N times and says how long a frame took
//   quit
// --desk-socket PATH also serves the desk protocol (generation 1, os/desk.coax's) there, one JSON line
// a request: list, focused, screens, open, move, click, close (by handle) and shot; the rest are
// refused with code not_supported. Verse OS's session points CODER_DESK_SOCKET at it.
// Effects (sockets, descriptors, shared memory) are coax/platform/wayland-native.c; the protocol,
// every object and every decision is here.
#import "Basic";
#load "../coax/lib/sys/tool.coax";
#load "../coax/lib/sys/fs.coax";
#load "../coax/lib/sys/args.coax";
#load "wm.coax";
#load "xwm.coax";
#load "desk-buffer-policy.coax";
#load "desk-dmabuf.coax";

cxgpu_open :: (node: [] u8) -> int #foreign;
cxgpu_format :: (i: int, field: int) -> int #foreign;
cxgpu_device :: () -> int #foreign;
cxgpu_import :: (fd: int, w: int, h: int, stride: int, offset: int, fmt: int, hi: int, lo: int) -> int #foreign;
cxgpu_capture :: (slot: int) -> int #foreign;
cxgpu_read :: (slot: int, offset: int, out: [] u8) -> int #foreign;
cxgpu_drop :: (slot: int) -> int #foreign;
cxgpu_close :: () -> int #foreign;
cxgpu_stat :: (field: int) -> int #foreign;

cxwl_listen :: (path: [] u8) -> int #foreign;
cxwl_unlisten :: (path: [] u8) -> int #foreign;
cxwl_accept :: () -> int #foreign;
cxwl_recv :: (h: int, out: [] u8) -> int #foreign;
cxwl_fd_count :: () -> int #foreign;
cxwl_fd :: (i: int) -> int #foreign;
cxwl_send :: (h: int, s: [] u8, fd: int) -> int #foreign;
cxwl_hangup :: (h: int) -> int #foreign;
cxwl_close_fd :: (fd: int) -> int #foreign;
